@page
@model PortfolioManager.Web.Pages.Legal.PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
}

<div class="col-lg-9">
    <h1 class="h2 pb-2 mb-3 border-bottom">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Version @LegalSettings.BuiltInVersion</p>

    <p>
        This policy explains how @Model.OperatorWithAbn ("we", "us") handles personal information on @Model.SiteName.
        We follow the Australian Privacy Principles in the Privacy Act 1988.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your email address, your name if you give it, and your password (stored only as a
            one-way hash we cannot read back).</li>
        <li><strong>The records you enter or import:</strong> trades, holdings, dividends, bank transactions, invoices, bills,
            properties, tenants, clients, attachments and the other records the site keeps. These can include other people's
            details if you enter them.</li>
        <li><strong>Security and technical details:</strong> your internet address, your browser, and a log of sign-ins,
            wrong passwords and changes to your password, two-factor sign-in and API keys.</li>
        <li><strong>Messages you send us</strong>, such as support emails.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Please don't enter tax file numbers. The site doesn't need them, and we ask you not to store them here.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Why we use it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To run the site for you: storing your records, working out your reports and sending the emails you ask for.</li>
        <li>To keep accounts secure: checking sign-ins, stopping password guessing and warning you about unusual sign-ins.</li>
        <li>To answer your questions, fix problems and meet our legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell your information, we don't show advertising, and we don't use tracking or analytics cookies.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        The site uses only the cookies it needs to work: one that keeps you signed in, one that remembers which portfolio you
        picked, one that recognises your browser so we can warn you about sign-ins from new devices, and short-lived ones
        that protect forms and pass messages between pages. If the "I'm human" check is turned on, Cloudflare sets its own
        cookie on the sign-in and sign-up pages. If you turn on offline copies, pages are saved on your own device.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>
        Your records are kept in our database on a server @(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Legal.HostingLocation) ? "run by our hosting provider" : Model.Legal.HostingLocation!.Trim()),
        and in our backups.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We only share your information when you use a feature that needs it, when you ask us to, or when the law requires it:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>People you share a portfolio with</strong>, at the access level you choose.</li>
        <li><strong>The AI assistant and document reading</strong> send your question, the records it needs and any file you
            ask it to read to Anthropic in the United States.</li>
        <li><strong>Accounting software</strong> (Xero or MYOB) receives the journals you choose to send, and
            <strong>Navexa</strong> is contacted when you connect it to import your records.</li>
        <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> delivers the emails the site sends you.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> checks your internet address and browser on the sign-in and sign-up pages, if the
            "I'm human" check is turned on.</li>
        <li><strong>Share price providers</strong> are only sent share codes, never your details.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Some of these providers are overseas (for example Anthropic and Cloudflare in the United States, and Xero and MYOB
        may store data outside Australia). We use them only for the feature you choose to use.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">How we protect it</h2>
    <p>
        The site uses HTTPS, hashed passwords, optional two-factor sign-in, encrypted storage of the keys you connect to other
        services, limits on password guessing and a security log. Access to the server and database is restricted. If a
        data breach is likely to cause you serious harm, we will tell you and the Office of the Australian Information
        Commissioner as the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
        We keep your records while you have an account. If you ask us to close your account, we delete your records within
        30 days, except anything the law requires us to keep. Copies in backups are removed as those backups expire.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Seeing, correcting or deleting your information</h2>
    <p>
        You can see and change most of your information on the site. To ask for a copy of what we hold, a correction or
        deletion, or to make a privacy complaint, email <partial name="_Contact" model="Model" />. We will reply within 30 days.
        If you are not happy with our answer, you can complain to the
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints" rel="noopener">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy, we will show the new version on the site and ask you to agree to it.</p>
</div>
